# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=flags (Ebb and Flow), spec=paladin:holy,
# style=melee, view=1280x800, save=carried (behaves as fresh per #273 -- playbot's
# own port is per-run, so localStorage's origin never actually carries between
# invocations).
#
# First paladin:holy on any battleground this job has run (its one prior outing
# was mode=raid, style=wander), and the first time a pure healer kit has been
# given `melee` style anywhere: direction.md's #7 already found that
# `style=auto`'s restoration druid on this same map stood still and never healed
# (auto has no steering at all), but `melee` does steer -- straight at the
# nearest enemy -- and then presses whatever ability the bar shows `ready` first,
# without regard to what that ability actually does. For a holy paladin the bar
# is almost entirely heals, so this cell asks a different question than auto did:
# what does a healer that walks into enemy melee range and presses its own
# healing kit actually do to itself and its team, on the one map #7 already
# showed has an automatic flag-carry penalty for anyone caught standing near a
# dropped flag.
open
tap battleground
tap map:flags
targets
tap class:paladin:holy
shot class-picked
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot bg-start
state
ui
play melee 90
shot mid1
state
bill
wait 3
play melee 90
shot mid2
state
bill
wait 3
play melee 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
